message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Capacity Lens: information-theoretic capacity diagnostics for neural networks"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight PyTorch toolkit that answers two design questions with information-theoretic necessary
  conditions: how much capacity does a task require, and can a given architecture supply it? A bottleneck
  layer inserted after the representation makes "capacity" a measurable number; the requirement is read
  from a reference model's achieved error (Fano), which yields a sound exclusion rule (log K < R_IB means
  the bottleneck provably cannot carry the task) and a measured practical wall for sizing decisions.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "usecodeandaiforstudy"
version: "0.6.1"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - information theory
  - capacity
  - quantization
  - knowledge distillation
  - vector quantization
  - Fano inequality
  - model compression
  - interpretability
